Kiekmap
=======

Kalle Erlhoff — idea, development, the museum side

Whoever contributes something adds themselves here. The rights holder is named in NOTICE, the terms
in LICENSE; an entry here changes neither.

How the project came about
--------------------------

Kiekmap was built with the help of an AI assistant; the commits carry that as Co-Authored-By. What
is produced purely by machine is not protected by copyright — what is protected is the work of
selection and arrangement, and that lies open in the reasoned decisions under docs/decisions.md.
The claim therefore goes no further than that: a copyright line, not the sentence "every line is my
work". At length in docs/licensing.md.

Third-party components
----------------------

The map comes from OpenStreetMap, the fonts from the Noto Project, the sprites from
protomaps/basemaps-assets. They are named in NOTICE; the full licence texts of every bundled
package are produced at build time as THIRD-PARTY.txt.
